# Rust
target/
target
/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is committed (Rust convention for binary-shipping
# workspaces: guarantees reproducible builds + the Docker install
# path's `COPY Cargo.toml Cargo.lock ./` requires it in the build
# context).

# Node
# No trailing slash: with one the pattern matches directories only, and
# infra/dev/wt-web links a worktree's node_modules to the operator's as
# SYMLINKS, which are not directories to the ignore rules — so the
# pattern that hid a bun install left three untracked paths in every
# builder worktree (backlog ef4394e1, 2026-09-14). Pinned in wt_web_sh.rs.
node_modules
dist/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code — everything under .claude/ is per-machine (worktrees,
# settings.local.json, locks) EXCEPT the project settings, which ship
# the hooks that make a session a work-session packet (design 511fa7d4
# car 2b, backlog da925366; pinned by dev_hooks_sh.rs), and the agent
# definitions, which are the CONTROL a step's declared effort selects
# (backlog e720dd00; pinned by boss_jobs::agent_spec's tests).
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md

# Build artifacts
*.log

# Playwright artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/

# TLA+ tooling — downloaded on demand by infra/tla/run-tlc.sh
infra/tla/tla2tools.jar
# TLC writes states/ alongside the spec when checking; .toolbox/
# is the IDE state from the official TLA+ Toolbox.
docs/formal/states/
docs/formal/*.toolbox/
**/__pycache__/

# Generated seed bundles — `infra/postgres/regenerate-brewery-seed.sh`
# rebuilds them from source (JobKinds + tenant.toml + the live sim).
# Don't commit; runtime consumers (the container launcher,
# reset-to-baseline.sh, oss-quickstart/init.sh) fetch or regenerate
# as needed. Keeps git history slim and forces every deployment to
# start from a known-fresh artifact rather than a stale snapshot.
infra/postgres/seed-brewery-audit-log.sql.gz
infra/postgres/seed-brewery-audit-log.meta.json

# The gate writes its own account of each run (infra/gate.sh
# write_receipt). It is evidence to paste onto a car, not a
# tracked artifact.
.gate-receipt.json
